    "created_at": "2016-03-02T08:12:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-02T08:12:33Z",
    "body": "Yeah, English removes spaces and hyphens over time. Wherever that's likely to happen, we should stick with the term English likely ends up with, thus, \"whitespace\", not \"white space\" or \"white-space\". And ideally we do this before implementations ship something (see \"fullscreen\").\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
